    "text": "Recommended values:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"causa\": \"C2\",\n  \"reverter\": \"recibos\",\n  \"reprocessar\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\"],\n  \"perda_confirmada\": false\n}\n```\n\nEvidence supports a consumer compatibility break: `recibos` v8 deployed at 14:05 began requiring `customer_id`, but the current producer contract supplies `cliente_id`. Local rejections began at 14:06. At 14:16, ten test messages in the existing format were accepted by one instance reverted to v7 using the same database and network. Remaining v8 instances still need rollback.\n\nQ1 contains 42 affected messages and Q2 contains 17. All 59 rejected messages are intact in the failure queue with original IDs and available payloads. These are messages, not retry attempts. Q3 consumed and acknowledged normally; Q4 was empty from 13:50 and received no events during the window. Neither belongs in the replay list.\n\nThe 14:08 alert is an aggregated, rounded signal and does not establish defect onset. The 13:40 dashboard change did not alter aggregation. C1 is weakened by the 14:12 database verification: available connections, stable latency, and successful reads/writes. That snapshot alone cannot exclude every earlier transient, but the schema mismatch and rollback result provide stronger causal evidence. C3 relies on a 14:04 laboratory DNS failure involving a resolver different from production, so it does not demonstrate production DNS unavailability.\n\nBefore replay, revert all `recibos` instances to v7 and validate a sample. Replay Q1 and Q2 while preserving original message IDs and their idempotency keys. `perda_confirmada=false` means no definitive loss is confirmed: retention is established, while complete recovery remains unverified because a full replay has not been validated.",
