    "thread_id": "01a12c64-d1f0-7fa0-960c-2f57452378d7",
    "kind": "subagent_final",
    "text": "Recommended values:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"causa\": \"C2\",\n  \"reverter\": \"recibos\",\n  \"reprocessar\": [\"Q1\", \"Q2\"],\n  \"perda_confirmada\": false\n}\n```\n\nThe v8 consumer introduced a requirement for `customer_id` while the producer still sends `cliente_id`. Deployment at 14:05 precedes matching local rejections at 14:06. The rollback experiment is decisive supporting evidence: v7 accepted ten current-contract messages using the same database and network.\n\nRevert remaining `recibos` instances from v8 to v7, validate a sample, then replay Q1 and Q2 in their listed order while preserving original IDs and idempotency keys. Q3 operated normally; Q4 was empty.\n\nC1 is weakened by available database connections and normal read/write behavior at 14:12. C3 is weakened because the DNS failure belonged to a laboratory probe using a different resolver. Producer rollback adds coordination without addressing the demonstrated consumer regression.\n\nAll 59 rejected messages remain intact, so permanent loss is not confirmed. Recovery remains unverified until complete replay succeeds; the ten-message test and point-in-time database check do not establish full recovery.",
